1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:03,770
You're hearing my voice, not a synthetic one.

2
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:10,570
I read this script out loud, once, and Lyceum timed every animation to my words.

3
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:15,790
That matters when the video is yours to present: a talk, a demo,

4
00:00:15,990 --> 00:00:17,310
an update for your team.

5
00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:20,890
People listen differently to someone they know.

6
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:28,050
Lyceum puts each element on screen at the moment its words are spoken.

7
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:32,250
A synthetic voice reads the script exactly, scene by scene.

8
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:34,150
A person doesn't.

9
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:35,650
I pause to think.

10
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:38,170
I say something that isn't in the script.

11
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:40,710
Sometimes I trip over a line.

12
00:00:41,890 --> 00:00:46,850
And recording every scene separately makes the whole thing sound stitched together.

13
00:00:49,183 --> 00:00:52,303
So I record the whole talk in one go.

14
00:00:53,323 --> 00:00:57,263
Lyceum listens to it and matches every word to the script.

15
00:00:57,703 --> 00:01:02,283
Then it cuts the take into scenes, in the pauses between them.

16
00:01:03,143 --> 00:01:09,523
Anything I say between scenes, like next slide, falls in a gap and is dropped.

17
00:01:10,183 --> 00:01:13,723
Each scene is trimmed, and brought to the same volume.

18
00:01:16,083 --> 00:01:21,143
If I stumble, Lyceum tells me which scene, and which words it didn't hear.

19
00:01:21,483 --> 00:01:26,243
I record just that scene again, and it replaces that part of the take.

20
00:01:26,923 --> 00:01:29,003
Everything else stays as it was.

21
00:01:29,663 --> 00:01:33,203
If I say something the script doesn't have, it keeps the audio,

22
00:01:33,203 --> 00:01:36,803
but warns me, because the captions won't show it.

23
00:01:39,183 --> 00:01:46,323
To narrate a video yourself, add one line to the script, saying the voice is recorded.

24
00:01:47,023 --> 00:01:49,843
Record the whole talk into the recordings folder.

25
00:01:50,083 --> 00:01:54,743
Then run narrate, just as you would with a synthetic voice.

26
00:01:55,563 --> 00:01:58,823
This video started as one take.

27
00:01:59,023 --> 00:02:01,783
Everything you just watched is timed to it.
